+    doc: 'The capability rail: a real frame column between the sidebar and the\ncentre, sized by the same solve that sizes the other tracks (48px strip\nor 320px panel). Its occupant draws inside that track — unlike\n`shell.overlay`, it never covers the sidebar\'s pixels.\n\nThe frame owns the open request and passes it in: occupants render from\n`open` and call `onToggle` to collapse/expand. The solve may still\nresolve an expanded request to the 48px strip on a frame too narrow to\nkeep the center\'s protected minimum; `open` reports that resolved state,\nnever the raw request. Drawer mode mounts no rail column at all.',
     registerOptions: [],
     ownerProps: [
       '/** Capability rail owner share: the frame-held open state and its one control. */\nexport interface RailOwnerProps {\n  /**\n   * Resolved expanded state: true only while the solve gives the rail its\n   * 320px track. A request the frame is too narrow to honour reports false, so\n   * the occupant renders its 48px strip instead of a panel inside a strip.\n   */\n  open: boolean\n  /** Flip the frame\'s expand request (the collapse control, `Esc`, and the strip). */\n  onToggle: () => void\n}',
